Author: whycz <whyczz@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 17 03:04:53 2026 -0500

    feat(dogfood.2): bubble proof in the parallel drive — Pi and Muse, sibling unaffected
    
    For humans: the parallel drive now proves the blocked bubble in both engine forms — a seeded node blocks, its whole worker tree dies, and a fresh tree revives it after the human answer, while its sibling keeps moving and lands.
    
    For LLMs: test/dogfood-parallel.sh gains an embedded bubble drive: Pi form spawns real node/edge processes claiming real links (typed E_DECISION failure, one facts-only bubble, process-table death, fresh run-id/pid after resume); Muse form runs the real induct-node workflow in parallel against real bp3 (same blocked bubble, one block, fresh workflow with disjoint run-ids, old host agent count frozen). Sibling unaffected in both forms. make check green.

 test/dogfood-parallel.sh | 210 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 210 insertions(+)
